Additional dependencies
-----------------------

Other Rust dependencies declare their licenses in their package manifests.
The Talos source release contains workspace manifests; Cargo.lock is generated
during the build and is not tracked in the source archive. Each dependency
retains its own license and notices in its source package. In particular,
packages with a choice of licenses may be used under any license offered by
that package; this notice does not relicense them.

The dependency versions above were present in the generated Cargo.lock used
to prepare this candidate. Inspect the lockfile and Cargo metadata from the
actual product build for its complete resolved dependency set; versions may
differ when dependencies are resolved again.

Browser Worker runtime
----------------------
The standard Docker Worker bundles Browser Use 0.13.11 (MIT, copyright 2024
Gregor Zunic), Browser Harness 0.1.13, and Chromium supplied by Playwright 1.64.1.

The Web and Desktop clients bundle the noVNC 1.5.0 RFB library, copyright the
noVNC authors, under MPL-2.0. Corresponding library source is available at
https://github.com/novnc/noVNC/tree/v1.5.0 and the license text at
https://github.com/novnc/noVNC/blob/v1.5.0/LICENSE.txt. Talos uses the library
inside its existing interface; the standalone noVNC application and websockify
are not part of the Worker image.
Their original package licenses remain in the image's Python distribution
metadata and Chromium resources. The image's /opt/talos/browser/requirements.lock
identifies the exact Python dependency graph and artifact hashes. Desktop uses
its bundled Electron/Chromium; it does not install this Docker Python runtime.

The Docker Worker seccomp profile derives from github.com/moby/profiles
(Apache-2.0), upstream SHA256
6416b47770785a41ac59073cdc77d9fe98517df2799dc83ef207e622de3053f6,
with clone/setns/unshare allowances for Chromium user namespaces.
